{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nvector<int> parent, compSize;\n\nint findRoot(int v) {\n    if (parent[v] == v) return v;\n    return parent[v] = findRoot(parent[v]);\n}\n\nvoid unite(int a, int b) {\n    a = findRoot(a);\n    b = findRoot(b);\n    if (a == b) return;\n    if (compSize[a] < compSize[b]) {\n        int t = a;\n        a = b;\n        b = t;\n    }\n    compSize[a] += compSize[b];\n    parent[b] = a;\n}\n\nll modPow(ll a, ll b) {\n    ll res = 1;\n    while (b) {\n        if (b & 1) res = res * a % MOD;\n        a = a * a % MOD;\n        b >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nll check(ll a, ll b, ll p) {\n    ll res = 1;\n    while (b) {\n        if (b & 1) res = res * a % p;\n        a = a * a % p;\n        b >>= 1;\n    }\n    return (res == 1) ? p : 1;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int p, k;\n    scanf(\"%d%d\", &p, &k);\n\n    if (k == 0) {\n        printf(\"%lld\", modPow(p, p - 1));\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    parent.resize(p);\n    compSize.assign(p, 1);\n    for (int i = 0; i < p; ++i) parent[i] = i;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < p; ++i) {\n        int nxt = (int)((k * 1LL * i) % p);\n        unite(nxt, i);\n    }\n\n    ll ans = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < p; ++i) {\n        if (findRoot(i) == i) {\n            ans = ans * check(k, compSize[i], p) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\", ans);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.util.StringTokenizer;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n    static int[] parent;\n    static int[] compSize;\n\n    static int findRoot(int v) {\n        if (parent[v] == v) return v;\n        return parent[v] = findRoot(parent[v]);\n    }\n\n    static void unite(int a, int b) {\n        a = findRoot(a);\n        b = findRoot(b);\n        if (a == b) return;\n        if (compSize[a] < compSize[b]) {\n            int t = a;\n            a = b;\n            b = t;\n        }\n        compSize[a] += compSize[b];\n        parent[b] = a;\n    }\n\n    static long modPow(long a, long b) {\n        long res = 1;\n        while (b > 0) {\n            if ((b & 1) == 1) res = res * a % MOD;\n            a = a * a % MOD;\n            b >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static long check(long a, long b, long p) {\n        long res = 1;\n        while (b > 0) {\n            if ((b & 1) == 1) res = res * a % p;\n            a = a * a % p;\n            b >>= 1;\n        }\n        return (res == 1) ? p : 1;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        int p = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        int k = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n\n        if (k == 0) {\n            System.out.println(modPow(p, p - 1));\n            return;\n        }\n\n        parent = new int[p];\n        compSize = new int[p];\n        for (int i = 0; i < p; ++i) {\n            parent[i] = i;\n            compSize[i] = 1;\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < p; ++i) {\n            int nxt = (int)((k * 1L * i) % p);\n            unite(nxt, i);\n        }\n\n        long ans = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < p; ++i) {\n            if (findRoot(i) == i) {\n                ans = ans * check(k, compSize[i], p) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -4.339123915997334e-05, -7.748573807475623e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.5759429931640625, -0.6953188180923462, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0788908526301384, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.029754003509879112, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00033563701435923576, -0.0045485603623092175, 0.0, -0.0011712603736668825, -1.8000440832111053e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.02095406875014305, -0.004082797560840845, -9.989239333663136e-05, -0.0489879846572876, -0.0007333449902944267, -0.008614521473646164, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.006716177798807621, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.054928455501794815, -0.00020346954988781363, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.5523738915799186e-05, -4.172238186583854e-05, 0.0, -0.20141683518886566, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, 0.0, -4.792098479811102e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.003185200970619917, 0.0, -0.014211166650056839, -4.410734163684538e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.861018856492592e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -8.22540732769994e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.000335398683091